---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Nav from '../../components/Nav.astro';
import Faq from '../../components/Faq.astro';
import Footer from '../../components/Footer.astro';
import SiteScripts from '../../components/SiteScripts.astro';
import '../../styles/category-article.css';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="How category leaders win | In The Kitchen"
  description="Category leadership comes from compounding advantages and the integrity of the decisions beneath your positioning."
  bodyClass="body-new category-article-page"
>
  <div class="page-wrapper">
    <Nav />

    <main class="category-article-main">
      <section class="category-article-hero" aria-labelledby="category-article-heading">
        <article class="category-article-card">
          <header class="category-article-header">
            <h1 id="category-article-heading">
              <span>You don’t create category</span>
              <span>leadership by being a little bit better.</span>
              <span class="category-article-heading-break">You do it by being</span>
              <span>fundamentally different.</span>
            </h1>
            <div class="category-article-meta" aria-label="Article details">
              <div class="category-article-reading-meta">
                <span>4 min read</span>
                <button class="category-article-listen" type="button" aria-pressed="false">
                  <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" aria-hidden="true">
                    <path d="M4 14v-2a8 8 0 0 1 16 0v2" />
                    <path d="M4 14h2v5H4a2 2 0 0 1-2-2v-1a2 2 0 0 1 2-2Z" />
                    <path d="M20 14h-2v5h2a2 2 0 0 0 2-2v-1a2 2 0 0 0-2-2Z" />
                  </svg>
                  <span class="category-article-listen-label">Listen</span>
                </button>
              </div>
              <div class="category-article-author">
                <span class="category-article-author-portrait" aria-hidden="true">
                  <img src="/assets/jon-itkin-byline.png" alt="" width="40" height="40" />
                </span>
                <span>By Jon Itkin</span>
              </div>
            </div>
          </header>

          <div class="category-article-rule" aria-hidden="true"></div>

          <div class="category-article-copy">
            <p>People will tell you positioning is a game of inches. Category leaders disagree. They drive compounding advantages across four dimensions, and product capabilities are only one.</p>
            <p>We use the Four Cs heuristic to deeply understand why you win. Then we channel our learnings into positioning and messaging that hits the market like a pile driver.</p>
            <h2>The four sources of competitive advantage:</h2>
          </div>

          <div class="category-article-four-cs">
            <section>
              <h3>Capability</h3>
              <p>What your buyers can do (and not do) as a result of your product.</p>
            </section>
            <section>
              <h3>Credibility</h3>
              <p>What makes you exceptionally trustworthy.</p>
            </section>
            <section>
              <h3>Convenience</h3>
              <p>Why it’s easier to buy from you.</p>
            </section>
            <section>
              <h3>Cost</h3>
              <p>Why you deliver outstanding value relative to investment.</p>
            </section>
          </div>
        </article>
      </section>

      <section class="category-article-quote" aria-label="Client testimonial">
        <figure>
          <blockquote>
            <p>“Jon helped us execute a crucial strategic repositioning and build a message that we fully own. Within weeks of launching, we closed our first enterprise deal and built a deep pipeline. The ideas and language we co-created are pulling the company forward.”</p>
          </blockquote>
          <figcaption>Alex Gallego, CEO, Redpanda</figcaption>
        </figure>
      </section>

      <section class="category-article-decisions" aria-labelledby="category-decisions-heading">
        <article class="category-article-card category-decisions-card">
          <div class="category-decisions-headlines">
            <h2 id="category-decisions-heading">
              <span>Marketing copy doesn’t</span>
              <span>make you a category leader.</span>
            </h2>
            <h2>Decisions do.</h2>
          </div>
          <div class="category-article-rule" aria-hidden="true"></div>
          <div class="category-article-copy">
            <p>After more than 45 deep-dive positioning exercises, we’ve learned that the most important factor behind positioning success is the integrity of the decisions beneath it.</p>
            <p>So we developed Decision-Based Positioning: a methodology that treats decisions as a first-class deliverable of the positioning process.</p>
            <p>With us, executives spend time debating crucial decisions, not splitting hairs over headlines. You leave with conviction about the path you’re taking, not just what you will say.</p>
            <h2>Decisions to win:</h2>
          </div>
          <ul class="category-decisions-list">
            <li><span>Intentions</span><span>7 decisions</span></li>
            <li><span>Playing Field</span><span>4 decisions</span></li>
            <li><span>Market Segment</span><span>3 decisions</span></li>
            <li><span>Buyer</span><span>4 decisions</span></li>
            <li><span>Problem</span><span>3 decisions</span></li>
            <li><span>Alternatives</span><span>3 decisions</span></li>
            <li><span>Advantages</span><span>5 decisions</span></li>
            <li><span>How You Win</span><span>2 decisions</span></li>
          </ul>
        </article>
      </section>
    </main>

    <Faq />
    <Footer />
  </div>

  <SiteScripts />
  <script is:inline>
    (() => {
    const listenButton = document.querySelector('.category-article-listen');

    if (listenButton && 'speechSynthesis' in window && 'SpeechSynthesisUtterance' in window) {
      const listenLabel = listenButton.querySelector('.category-article-listen-label');
      const article = document.querySelector('.category-article-main');
      let activeUtterance = null;

      const resetListenButton = () => {
        activeUtterance = null;
        listenButton.setAttribute('aria-pressed', 'false');
        if (listenLabel) listenLabel.textContent = 'Listen';
      };

      listenButton.addEventListener('click', () => {
        if (activeUtterance) {
          window.speechSynthesis.cancel();
          resetListenButton();
          return;
        }

        const articleText = article?.innerText.trim() ?? '';
        if (!articleText) return;

        activeUtterance = new window.SpeechSynthesisUtterance(articleText);
        activeUtterance.rate = 0.95;
        activeUtterance.onend = resetListenButton;
        activeUtterance.onerror = resetListenButton;
        listenButton.setAttribute('aria-pressed', 'true');
        if (listenLabel) listenLabel.textContent = 'Stop';
        window.speechSynthesis.speak(activeUtterance);
      });

      window.addEventListener('pagehide', () => {
        if (activeUtterance) window.speechSynthesis.cancel();
      });
    } else if (listenButton) {
      listenButton.hidden = true;
    }
    })();
  </script>
</BaseLayout>
